{
  "about": [
    "Prose-level watchlist for physics-shaped and outside-target vocabulary. Terms are stored as SHA-256 digests of their normalized form (NFKD, combining marks dropped, lowercase) so that this repository never carries the words themselves as prose. CLAUDE.md records a refused outside grid on exactly that ground: describe, do not name.",
    "This is a CENSUS, not a denylist. Every whole-word hit in tracked prose is pinned per file under 'baseline'. A hit above its pinned count fails by file, line, and surface token; a hit below it fails as a stale pin; '--regen' rewrites the pin deliberately. The pin puts the tree's physics-shaped vocabulary in one inspectable place instead of leaving it native-looking in many.",
    "Digests are not secrets: 'python ci/check_prose_watchlist.py --probe WORD' says whether a word is watched. A token matches if it, or it minus a trailing s or es, digests to a watched term; two-word terms match adjacent tokens on one line. Identifiers with underscores or digits are never split, so this gate reads prose and the identifier firewall keeps identifiers.",
    "Out of scope: prompt/prompt.md and prompt/seed_prompt.md (the read-only seed inputs, the one place outside terms are permitted), the contact/analysis/ quarantine (the identifier firewall excludes it for the same reason), this file, and any file containing a NUL byte.",
    "Class tags: 'physics-shaped common noun' (counted, never refused; several are house words in research/), 'outside proper name', and 'outside program phrase (two words)'."
  ],
